  "synthesis": {
    "description": "A budget coordinator opens the round by sending managers a budget questionnaire with a return deadline (the first draft of the 2001 budget was due on September 18th). Managers fill in salary, staffing and training figures, sometimes after checking headcount and pay with HR, and send back revised forecasts. The coordinator loads each return into the budget spreadsheets to build the draft; small regions answer briefly, offering a single salary on request.",
    "steps": [
      "The coordinator sends the budget questionnaire to managers with a due date for the first draft.",
      "Each manager gathers salary, staffing and training figures for their group, checking with HR where needed.",
      "Managers return the completed questionnaire or a revised budget forecast as an attachment.",
      "Managers send further revisions after reviewing the numbers again.",
      "The coordinator enters every return into the budget spreadsheets to assemble the draft."
    ],
    "approach": "Replace the free-form questionnaire with a fixed budget input form per manager, prefilled from HR headcount and current salaries, that feeds directly into the consolidation spreadsheet so the coordinator no longer retypes returns and revisions overwrite cleanly.",
    "rationale": "The work centres on collecting the same salary, staffing and training fields from many managers and keying them into spreadsheets; a standard prefilled input layout removes the retyping and the back-and-forth with HR, while managers still judge the forecast.",
    "artifact_type": "template"
  },
